Persistent Context: Use CLAUDE.md files to store project-specific rules so you don't have to repeat yourself in every session.
2️⃣ The "Plan First" Rule: Don't let the agent dive into code immediately. Force a solution plan and use the built-in "to-do list" feature to track progress.
3️⃣ Session Hygiene: Keep context windows lean. Use /compact or /clear to ensure the model stays sharp on the current task.
4️⃣ CLI Superpowers: Integrate MCP servers and custom CLI tools. The more tools you give it, the more "agentic" it becomes.
5️⃣ Multi-Instance Orchestration: For complex builds, the pros are now running multiple Claude instances simultaneously or using headless mode for CI/CD.
6️⃣ Visual Debugging: Stuck on a UI bug? Feed it a screenshot. Claude Code’s multimodal capability bridges the gap between code and pixels.
7️⃣ Test-Driven AI: Make linting, TDD, and regular commits part of the automated workflow for cleaner repos.
8️⃣ The Kill Switch: Master the 'Escape' key. Real-time intervention is the secret to guiding an agent when it veers off-course.


